 ◆ Done. The issue was one line ("Make the booking flow better"), so I read the existing web booking flow end to end and fixed the three places where it actually breaks for a user,
 ▎ rather than inventing new features.
 ▎ 
 ▎ ▌ What I changed
 ▎ 
 ▎ apps/web/src/components/booking/steps/PaymentStep.tsx — closing the Razorpay window left the sheet on a spinner that never finished ("Preparing payment…"). The root cause
 ▎ was that "idle" meant both "about to auto-open Razorpay" and "user closed Razorpay, now waiting". I split those with a dismissed flag: the dismissed state renders "Payment was
 ▎ cancelled. Your tickets are still held." with Pay again / Back to review, and the auto-start effect no longer re-opens Razorpay behind the user's back.
 ▎ 
 ▎ apps/web/src/components/booking/steps/ReviewStep.tsx — the "Edit details" pencil jumped to step 3 unconditionally, but AttendeesStep auto-skips straight back to Review when
 ▎ the event has no attendee fields, so the button read as broken. It now routes to step 3 only when visibleSteps.includes(3) (the shared getVisibleBookingSteps contract), else to
 ▎ the ticket step, and the aria-label follows.

 ▎ apps/web/src/components/booking/steps/SelectStep.tsx — the progress breadcrumb was missing from the ticket-selection screen in all three render branches (loading skeleton, RSVP,
 ▎ normal), so it vanished halfway through checkout. Added <BookingStepper currentStep="tickets" /> to each, matching what apps/mobile already does in the same three places.

 ▎ CHANGELOG.md — three lines under [Unreleased] → Fixed.

